function cmpNote(){var r=[['k','ㄱ','g / k','ㅋ','strong k','ㄲ','kk'],['t','ㄷ','d / t','ㅌ','strong t','ㄸ','tt'],['p','ㅂ','b / p','ㅍ','strong p','ㅃ','pp'],['ch','ㅈ','j','ㅊ','ch','ㅉ','jj']];
  var rows=r.map(function(x){return '<tr><td>'+x[0]+'</td><td><b>'+x[1]+'</b><small>'+x[2]+'</small></td><td><b>'+x[3]+'</b><small>'+x[4]+'</small></td><td><b>'+x[5]+'</b><small>'+x[6]+'</small></td></tr>'}).join('');
  return '<details class="cmp"><summary>Note: plain, aspirated, tense</summary><p>Many consonants come in 3 strengths. The place in your mouth is the same. Only the air and the tightness change.</p><table><tr><th></th><th>Plain</th><th>Aspirated</th><th>Tense</th></tr>'+rows+'<tr><td>s</td><td><b>ㅅ</b><small>s</small></td><td>—</td><td><b>ㅆ</b><small>ss</small></td></tr></table><p><b>Plain:</b> soft, a little air.<br><b>Aspirated:</b> a strong puff of air.<br><b>Tense:</b> tight throat, no air.</p><p class="tip">Hold a tissue in front of your mouth. It moves a lot for ㅋ ㅌ ㅍ ㅊ. It barely moves for ㄱ ㄷ ㅂ ㅈ. It stays still for ㄲ ㄸ ㅃ ㅉ.</p></details>'}
function posNote(){var all=C.concat(D);
  var rows=all.map(function(x){return '<tr><td><b>'+x[0]+'</b></td><td>'+x[4][0]+'</td><td>'+x[4][1]+'</td><td>'+x[4][2]+'</td></tr>'}).join('');
  return '<details class="cmp"><summary>Note: sounds change by position</summary><p>A consonant can sound different at the start, in the middle, and at the bottom of a block.</p><table><tr><th></th><th>Start</th><th>Middle</th><th>End</th></tr>'+rows+'</table>'
  +'<p><b>ㄱ ㄷ ㅂ</b> at the start are soft: g, d, b. Some people hear them close to k, t, p.</p>'
  +'<p><b>ㄹ</b> at the start is l, and it is used mostly in loan words. Between vowels it is r. At the bottom it is l. ㄹㄹ sounds like l.</p>'
  +'<p><b>ㅅ</b> sounds like sh before ㅣ ㅑ ㅕ ㅛ ㅠ ㅒ ㅖ ㅟ. Before other vowels it is s. Example: 시 is shi, 사 is sa.</p>'
  +'<p><b>ㅈ</b> at the start is a low ch, between j and ch.</p>'
  +'<p><b>ㅎ</b> in the middle is often not clearly said.</p>'
  +'<p><b>ㅇ</b> is silent at the start and ng at the bottom.</p>'
  +'</details>'}
